        "answer": "Compare context-selection strategies against one fixed baseline, candidate configuration, manifest, environment, request set, and holdout set. Measure: (1) irrelevant-material rate: selected tokens or items judged irrelevant divided by total selected; (2) relevant-coverage rate: required relevant items selected divided by all required items; (3) deterministic repeatability: identical envelope digests across repeated runs; (4) provenance completeness: required source IDs, digests, selectors, and transformations present; (5) cache-reuse correctness: reuse decisions matching exact dependency and epoch comparisons; and (6) cost: tokens, latency, and selection work. Use paired requests so each strategy sees identical inputs. Record item-level inclusion/exclusion decisions, relevance reasons, ordered context IDs, digests, and blocker states. Evaluate on a fixed holdout set, report aggregate metrics plus failures, and preserve raw receipts sufficient to reproduce every comparison. A strategy should be considered promising only when it reduces irrelevant material without lowering required coverage or provenance completeness, while maintaining deterministic outputs. This is a measurement and research plan only; it does not implement, approve, admit, publish, deploy, or authorize any strategy."
